# Line endings are LF in the repository, on every platform.
#
# Without this file, a clone made on Windows with core.autocrlf=true commits
# CRLF, and two CI jobs fail in ways that look like content problems and are
# not:
#
#   - `prettier --check` defaults to endOfLine "lf" and flags every file.
#   - `packages/schemas/scripts/generate.mjs --check` compares the generated
#     text against the file on disk. The generator writes LF, so on a CRLF
#     checkout every generated file reads as stale no matter what it says.
#
# Both are decided by bytes the author never typed, so they are fixed here
# rather than by weakening either check. Developers on Windows keep working
# as before -- git converts on checkout only if they ask it to, and nothing
# in the toolchain needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never converted. `text=auto` detects most of these on its own; they
# are listed because a corrupted checkpoint or capture is expensive to notice
# and the cost of being explicit is one line each.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.glb binary
*.gltf binary
*.ply binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.pt binary
